     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi again!<div><br></div><div>Does anyone know, will the whole session today be about vegan, or will there also be time to work on our own projects?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks, hope you&#39;re all enjoying the tule fog!</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>El jueves, 4 de diciembre de 2014 15:01:31 UTC-8, Noam Ross escribió:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Next week at D-RUG, Tim Bowles will teach a short workshop on the <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/vegan/index.html\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/vegan/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468509283000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MjV5yR7Bjnc1szP_gcidK\"><em>vegan</em></a> package.  From Tim: </p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:1em 0px;border-left-width:4px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(221,221,221);padding:0px 1em;color:rgb(119,119,119);quotes:none\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\"><strong>Getting into the meat of <em>vegan</em></strong> (yup, that was intended): Do you work with community and environment data? Or did you measure too many variables that are more or less related to each other and need to wade through them? Or have data with a lot more variables than samples (e.g. gene expression, spectroscopy)? Then <em>vegan</em>, a package for community analysis, might be useful for you. While <em>vegan</em> was designed with analysis of species/environment relationships in mind, it’s useful anytime you want to implement many standard multivariate techniques in R.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">I will walk through some of the basics of vegan, including: how to do ordination (PCA and NMDS); relating community data to environmental variables through constrained ordination (RDA) and vector overlaying; and permutational analysis of variance. I will also go over dissecting vegan’s ordination output to produce pretty graphs that are publication ready. <em>vegan</em> also has functions for analysis of biodiversity (e.g. calculation of diversity indices, species abundance models) but I will not cover them. </p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">We’ll meet at the regular time and place (Tuesday 1:10-3, Wickson 2124*), and of course, there will be cookies.  We will also screencast the talk at this link: <a href=\"http://goo.gl/S2iIn8\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://goo.gl/S2iIn8&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468509283000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3HVOFh97L-or98Rp-QlRj3\">http://goo.gl/S2iIn8</a>, though I have yet to successfully cookie-cast.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">*Wheelchair accessible via ramp at main entrance, elevators at East and West sides of building.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:SGkgYWxsLDxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+TmV4dCB3ZWVrIGF0IEQtUlVHLCBUaW0gQm93bGVz\r\nIHdpbGwgdGVhY2ggYSBzaG9ydCB3b3Jrc2hvcCBvbiB0aGUgWyp2ZWdhbipdKGh0dHA6Ly9jcmFu\r\nLnItcHJvamVjdC5vcmcvd2ViL3BhY2thZ2VzL3ZlZ2FuL2luZGV4Lmh0bWwpIHBhY2thZ2UuICZu\r\nYnNwO0Zyb20gVGltOiZuYnNwOzwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGRpdiBzdHlsZT0i\r\nbGluZS1oZWlnaHQ6IDE5Ljc5OTk5OTIzNzA2MDVweDsiPiZndDsqKkdldHRpbmcgaW50byB0aGUg\r\nbWVhdCBvZiAqdmVnYW4qKio8aT4mbmJzcDs8L2k+KHl1cCwgdGhhdCB3YXMgaW50ZW5kZWQpOiBE\r\nbyB5b3Ugd29yayB3aXRoIGNvbW11bml0eSBhbmQgZW52aXJvbm1lbnQgZGF0YT8gT3IgZGlkIHlv\r\ndSBtZWFzdXJlIHRvbyBtYW55IHZhcmlhYmxlcyB0aGF0IGFyZSBtb3JlIG9yIGxlc3MgcmVsYXRl\r\nZCB0byBlYWNoIG90aGVyIGFuZCBuZWVkIHRvIHdhZGUgdGhyb3VnaCB0aGVtPyBPciBoYXZlIGRh\r\ndGEgd2l0aCBhIGxvdCBtb3JlIHZhcmlhYmxlcyB0aGFuIHNhbXBsZXMgKGUuZy4gZ2VuZSBleHBy\r\nZXNzaW9uLCBzcGVjdHJvc2NvcHkpPyBUaGVuJm5ic3A7KnZlZ2FuPGk+KjwvaT4sIGEgcGFja2Fn\r\nZSBmb3IgY29tbXVuaXR5IGFuYWx5c2lzLCBtaWdodCBiZSB1c2VmdWwgZm9yIHlvdS4gV2hpbGUm\r\nbmJzcDsqdmVnYW4qPGk+Jm5ic3A7PC9pPndhcyBkZXN